Vendored verbatim (MIT, see each file header) from torvalds/linux d89e1d1 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau by scratchpad tools/vendor.py.
Exceptions: nvkm/engine/device/base.c is trimmed to the nv12b (GM20B) chipset only;
include/nvif/os.h is not vendored (../shim/include/nvif/os.h replaces it).
nvkm/subdev/ltc/gm20b.c is not upstream: GM20B's compbit backing store after nvgpu's ltc_gm20b.c.
nvkm/engine/gr/gf100.c and gf100.h give every channel's context a zcull image of its own (ctxsw mode separate buffer, as
nvgpu's gr_gk20a_ctx_zcull_setup binds one), so the raw path's zcull regions hold across context switches.
nvkm/engine/gr/gk20a.c enables TEX exceptions next to SM ones in TPC_EXCEPTION_EN (0x419d0c = 0x3, nvgpu's value);
nvkm/engine/gr/gf100.c takes a trap with TEX exceptions alone as nvgpu does (gf100_gr_trap_tex, ../../TegraGM20BTexTrap.h):
reported with dev_warn, the ESR written back, no TRAP error and so no channel kill.
nvkm/engine/gr/gk20a.c floorsweeps (gf100_grctx_generate_floorsweep: SM ids, PD/DS TPC counts, ROP mapping) at every GR
init, as nvgpu's gk20a_init_gr_setup_hw calls init_fs_state at every power-on, not only for the golden context.
nvkm/engine/gr/gf100.c tells the kext of each channel error gf100_gr_intr reports, before acknowledging it
(tgm_gr_fault, ../../TegraGM20BGrFault.h), so the kill names the job GR stopped in.

